calamares (3.3.14-0ubuntu30oaxaca2) @BASE_SERIES@; urgency=medium

  * revert-device-on-gui-thread.patch: the partition page reverts the device
    and, in "Replace a partition", lays out the new partitions on the GUI
    thread instead of a worker thread, which reset the models the preview
    views were painting from. Choosing the free space and then confirming the
    encryption passphrase crashed Calamares with a segfault in
    PartitionModel::data() (Legion laptop, 2026-10-13; reproduced in QEMU).

 -- santisbon <santisbon@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:00:00 -0500

calamares (3.3.14-0ubuntu30oaxaca1) @BASE_SERIES@; urgency=medium

  * Ubuntu's 3.3.14-0ubuntu30 rebuilt for @DISTRO_NAME@ with one patch,
    replace-read-selection-before-revert.patch: in "Replace a partition", read
    the selected partition from the preview's index on the GUI thread before
    the worker reverts the device, instead of from the worker afterwards, when
    the index dangles. Calamares crashed when the encryption passphrase was
    confirmed after a partition had been selected (Legion laptop,
    2026-10-12). debian/ is otherwise Ubuntu's.

 -- santisbon <santisbon@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 12 Oct 2026 23:00:00 -0500
